"Metis - alexar76/aicom GitHub Wiki (https://github-wiki-see.page/m/alexar76/aicom/wiki/Metis)\nciteturn9search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; > Live demo: metis.modelmarket.dev · 3D landing: alexar76.github.io/metis · Source: github.com/alexar76/metis · PyPI: `aimarket-metis` · Factory integration: `docs/metis-integration.md`\n\n# Metis - alexar76/aicom GitHub Wiki\n\n# Metis — cognition & verification tier\n\nMetis (μῆτις) is the ecosystem's distributed cognitive layer over any LLM — Understanding Council → fail-closed confidence gate → layered Mixture-of-Agents → grounded verifier. It returns a machine-readable verification envelope (`verify_score`, `verified`, optional `needs_clarification`).\n\n> Live demo: metis.modelmarket.dev · 3D landing: alexar76.github.io/metis · Source: github.com/alexar76/metis · PyPI: `aimarket-metis` · Factory integration: `docs/metis-integration.md`\n\n## Why Metis matters in AICOM\n\nLayer  | Role\n--- | ---\nOracles  | Verifiable math primitives (randomness, VDF, reputation, …)\nMetis  | Verifiable cognition — multi-agent reasoning + confidence gate on natural-language decisions\nAI-Factory  | Produces products; optionally calls Metis on high-stakes stages (`architect`, `methodologist`)\nARGUS  | Demand-side agent; can consume Metis + MCP tools like any other host\n\nHard invariant: factory and Metis are independent. Missing Metis → factory runs unchanged (fail-open gate). Missing factory → Metis serves `/v1/*` normally.\n\n## Factory integration (optional gate)\n\nHigh-stakes pipeline stages can POST to Metis `/v1/verify` via `llm/metis_gate.py` (HTTP only — never imports `metis`).\n    \n    `export METIS_URL=https://metis.internal:8080   # default http://127.0.0.1:8080\n    export AIFACTORY_METIS_GATE=auto               # auto | on | off (default auto)\n    export AIFACTORY_METIS_GATE_BLOCK=0          # 1 = allow low-confidence to escalate\n    `\n\nFull env table + sequence diagrams: `docs/metis-integration.md` · RU · ES · FR · ZH\n\n## MCP tools (Metis as consumer)\n\nMetis agents can attach ecosystem MCP servers via presets:\n\nPreset  | Server  | Tools\n--- | --- | ---\n`aimarket-oracle-gateway`  | aimarket-oracle-gateway  | 35 verifiable oracle tools\n`aimarket-web`  | aimarket-mcp  | `web_fetch`, `web_search`, `metis_verify` (SSRF-hardened)\n    \n    `enable_mcp_tools: true\n    mcp_ecosystem_presets:\n      - aimarket-oracle-gateway\n      - aimarket-web\n    `\n\naimarket-mcp — shared MCP gateway (stdio on Glama, HTTP self-host). Written once; consumed by Metis, ARGUS, and any stdio/HTTP MCP host.\n\nMetis-side doc: `metis/docs/en/ECOSYSTEM.md`\n\n## Alien Monitor\n\nMetis appears as the `cognition` node in Alien Monitor — live stats + in-graph chat proxied server-side (`POST /api/metis/chat`) so API keys never reach the browser.\n\n## Quick start (standalone)\n    \n    `git clone https://github.com/alexar76/metis.git && cd metis\n    pip install -e \".[dev,distributed]\"\n    metis-serve --port 8080\n    # OpenAPI: /v1/verify · /v1/chat/completions · /aimarket/invoke\n    `\n\nDocker: `docker compose up -d` in the metis repo.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n (https://glama.ai/mcp/servers/alexar76/aimarket-hub/tree)\nciteturn9search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 weeks ago;       <a href=\"https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-protocol\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/alexar76/aimarket-hub/refs/heads/main/docs/badges/aimarket.svg\" alt=\"Protocol\" /></a>\n      <a href=\"https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-hub/releases\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/alexar76/aimarket-hub/refs/heads/main/docs/badges/release.svg\" alt=\"Release\" /></a>\n      <a href=\"https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-protocol\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/alexar76/aimarket-hub/refs/heads/main/docs/badges/aimarket.svg\" alt=\"Protocol\" /></a>\n      <a href=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/alexar76/aimarket-hub/refs/heads/main/docs/badges/coverage.svg\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/alexar76/aimarket-hub/refs/heads/main/docs/badges/coverage.svg\" alt=\"Test coverage\" /></a>\n      <a href=\"https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-hub/blob/main/LICENSE\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/alexar76/aimarket-hub/refs/heads/main/docs/badges/license.svg\" alt=\"License: Apache-2.0\" /></a>\n    </p>\n    <!-- /aicom-readme-badges -->\n    \n    > 🌐 **English** · [Русский](docs/README.ru.md) · [Español](docs/README.es.md) · [Français](docs/README.fr.md) · [中文](docs/README.zh.md) · [Glossary](https://github.com/alexar76/aicom/blob/main/docs/localization-glossary.md)\nFull spec: [`../aimarket-protocol/spec.md`](https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-protocol/blob/main/spec.md)\n    \n    ## Invoke lifecycle\n    \n    Standard consumer flow (implemented by [`aimarket_agent`](https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-sdks/tree/main/dart/)):\n    \n    ```mermaid\n    sequenceDiagram\n      autonumber\n      participant Client\n      participant Hub as AIMarket Hub\n      participant Plugins\n      participant Target as Provider / local invoke\n    \n      Client->>Hub: search(intent, budget)\n      Hub-->>Client: plan[]\n    \n      Client->>Hub: channel/open(deposit_usd)\n      Hub-->>Client: channel_id\n    \n      Client->>Hub: invoke(capability_id, input, channel_id)\n      Hub->>Plugins: on_invoke_pre_check\n      alt rejected\n        Plugins-->>Hub: signed rejection\n        Hub-->>Client: 403 + channel refund\n      else ok\n        Hub->>Target: forward or local execute\n        Target-->>Hub: output, price_usd\n        Hub->>Plugins: on_invoke_post_check\n        Hub-->>Client: result + provenance_receipt\n    - **Vulnerability reports:** [SECURITY.md](https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-hub/blob/main/SECURITY.md) → alexar76@rambler.ru\n    \n    ## Related projects\n    \n    | Project | Relationship |\n    |---------|--------------|\n    | [AICOM / AI-Factory](https://github.com/alexar76/aicom/blob/main/README.md) | Ships products → hub index |\n    | [aimarket-protocol](https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-protocol/tree/main/) | Normative v2 spec |\n    | [aimarket-sdks](https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-sdks/tree/main/) | Client SDKs (Dart alpha) |\n    | [aimarket-widget](https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-widget/tree/main/) | Embeddable UI |\n    | [oracles](https://github.com/alexar76/oracles/tree/main/) | Verifiable math capabilities — randomness, VDF, consensus, reputation (listed on hub) |\n    | [desktop-integrations](https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-desktop/tree/main/) | 8 Flutter consumer apps |\n    | [Ecosystem architecture](https://github.com/alexar76/aicom/blob/main/docs/ecosystem-architecture.md) | Full monorepo diagram |\n    | [dioscuri](https://github.com/alexar76/dioscuri) | Twin community agents — MNEMOSYNE Q&A |\n    \n    ## Community\n    \n    The [DIOSCURI](https://github.com/alexar76/dioscuri) twins answer questions from synced GitHub docs.\n    \n    | Channel | Twin | Best for |\n    |---------|------|----------|\n    | [Discord](https://discord.gg/aimarket) | Pollux | Help, ideas, show-and-tell |\n    | [Telegram](https://t.me/just_for_agents) | Castor | Releases, digests, quick news |\n    \n    **Ecosystem map:** [Alien Monitor](https://monitor.modelmarket.dev/) · [AICOM](https://magic-ai-factory.com)\n    \n    ---\n    \n    ## License\n    \n    Apache-2.0 — see [LICENSE](https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-hub/blob/main/LICENSE). Maintainers: [CONTRIBUTORS.md](https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-hub/blob/main/CONTRIBUTORS.md).--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTHEMIS — Admit. Or don’t. Before the catalogue. (https://alexar76.github.io/themis/)\nciteturn9search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; $ `uvx create-aimarket-agent themis --kind tool --metis` [Button: COPY] ... capability `agent.security.supply-chain.audit@v1` MIT · a procurement aid, not a compliance certification alexar76.github.io/themis\n\nAIMarket · publish admission\n\n# Admit. Or don’t.\nBefore the catalogue.\n\nTHEMIS (Θέμις) is the signed publish-time gate: `approve` / `review` / `reject` from a bounded dossier — deterministic policy, request-bound Ed25519 receipt, no free crawl of the candidate. Not Metis (cognition). Not WARDEN (invoke-time firewall).\n\nSee it on Alien Monitor Open the console Rebuild from the mini-course\n\n$ `uvx create-aimarket-agent themis --kind tool --metis` [Button: COPY]\n\nAPPROVE catalogue path\n\nREVIEW human · Metis advisory\n\nREJECT fail closed\n\nWebGL is unavailable here. The gate logic is identical — read the signed verdicts below.\n\n3\n\nVerdicts\n\n84\n\nTests\n\n98%\n\nCoverage\n\nEd25519\n\nSigned receipt\n\n12\n\nCourse steps\n\n5\n\nLanguages\n\nCandidate → gate → receipt\n\n## One dossier in. One signed verdict out.\n\nThe policy engine decides immediately from identity, transport, permissions, cost, schemas and evidence shape. Metis may add an asynchronous second opinion — it never overrides the signed verdict. \nAlien Monitor admits nobody. It renders dossier-free admission telemetry after Hub has already recorded a receipt. Nothing on a public dashboard can grant catalogue access.\n\ncreate-aimarket-agent\n\n## Mini-course: build this agent yourself\n\nTHEMIS is the finished reference for the five-language create-aimarket-agent tutorial — twelve steps from an empty folder to a deliberate Hub publish, with the same 84 tests and the same fail-closed defaults you see above.\n\n### Generate\n\n`uvx create-aimarket-agent` · tool + Metis\n\n### Decide\n\nWrite the product decision before the code\n\n### Model\n\nStrict dossier, unknown fields rejected\n\n### Findings\n\nDeterministic policy → score → tier\n\n### Metis\n\nReal, lazy, non-blocking advisory\n\n### Sign\n\nCover the exact submitted input\n\n### Test\n\nBehaviour, not only happy paths\n\n### Scenario\n\nExercise the business case end to end\n\n### Poll\n\nRun Metis without blocking the user\n\n### Containerize\n\nLocked deps, unprivileged image\n\n### Publish\n\nAn explicit operator action\n\n### Done\n\nDefinition of done, then next exercises\n\nTHEMIS\n\nPublish-time admission gate for the AIMarket agent supply chain. MIT licensed reference implementation — read it, run it, rebuild it.\n\n##### Repository\n\nSource on GitHub Quick start Admission console Security boundary Verification\n\n##### Docs\n\nSupply-chain admission Architecture Full tutorial Русский · ES · FR · ZH\n\n##### Ecosystem\n\nAIMarket Alien Monitor THEMIS dashboards create-aimarket-agent OWASP Agentic Top 10\n\ncapability `agent.security.supply-chain.audit@v1` MIT · a procurement aid, not a compliance certification alexar76.github.io/themis--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nEcosystem - alexar76/aicom GitHub Wiki (https://github-wiki-see.page/m/alexar76/aicom/wiki/Ecosystem)\nciteturn9search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; # Ecosystem - alexar76/aicom GitHub Wiki ... School / Courses  | `school/` · `courses/`  | edu.modelmarket.dev · aimarket-courses\nGAIA  | `gaia/` → alexar76/gaia  | Physical-world oracle gateway — attested IoT + public-API relays · iot.modelmarket.dev\nATLAS  | `atlas/` → alexar76/atlas  | Planetary sensor map over GAIA (LIVE/SIM) · atlas.modelmarket.dev\nPlaton UMBRAL  | `platon/` → alexar76/platon  | Educational cave for oracle #1 · /platon/umbral\nProtocol v2  | `aimarket-protocol/`  | Normative spec, schemas, ecosystem diagrams\nHub plugins  | `plugins/` (15 pip packages)  | Safety, channels, TEE, reputation, orchestrator, …\nDesktop SKUs  | `desktop-integrations/`  | Flutter / Tauri / VS Code consumers on hub\nSDKs  | `aimarket-sdks/`  | Dart / TS / Rust clients\nBridges  | `aimarket-bridges/`  | LangGraph / CrewAI / AutoGen tools\nWidget  | `aimarket-widget/`  | Embeddable search + invoke\nContracts  | `contrac