ifier` attribution when a non-Metis verifier serves the slot\n`AIMARKET_APPEAL_WINDOW_S`  | `0`  | Appeals (protocol): seconds a genuine paid verdict stays provisional and appealable by the losing party. `0` = off, verdicts move money at once\n`AIMARKET_APPEAL_METIS_URL`  | —  | The appeal court: a second verifier. Unset, or equal to the first-instance URL, keeps appeals off\n`AIMARKET_APPEAL_METIS_KEY`  | —  | Appeal court bearer key\n`AIMARKET_APPEAL_VERIFIER_ID`  | `metis.appeal@v1`  | Names the appeal court in envelopes; must differ from `AIMARKET_VERIFY_VERIFIER_ID`\n`AIMARKET_APPEAL_BOND_MIN_USD` / `AIMARKET_APPEAL_BOND_RATE`  | `0.02` / `0.20`  | Bond = max(min, rate × price), capped at the price\n`AIMARKET_APPEAL_MAX_WAIT_S`  | `21600`  | After this the court counts as indeterminate: the first verdict stands, the bond is returned (`0` = no limit)\n`AIMARKET_APPEAL_SWEEP_S`  | `30`  | Safety-net pass that finalizes expired windows and picks up filed appeals\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHome - alexar76/aicom GitHub Wiki (https://github-wiki-see.page/m/alexar76/aicom/wiki)\nciteturn9search9 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month;     `git clone https://github.com/alexar76/aicom.git ... The wider AIMarket stack lives in sibling satellites: hub, protocol, desktop SKUs, plugins, widget, SDKs, oracles, GAIA/ATLAS, Metis, LOGOS, SKOPOS, MOMUS/Treasury, Signal Hunt, DIOSCURI/HELIOS/THEOROS, ACEX, mesh, and MCP servers.\nEcosystem & satellite repos  | Ecosystem\nVerifiable oracles  | Oracles\nMetis (cognition + verify)  | Metis · RU\nLOGOS (federation analytics)  | Logos\nSignal Hunt (investigation game)  | Signal-Hunt\nInstall and first product  | Quick-Start\nDeploy the full ecosystem  | Quick-Start-Ecosystem\nPlatform owner  | Owner-Guide\nPipeline, discovery, remediation  | Pipeline\nAdmin UI and roles  | Admin-Panel\nDocker / production  | Deployment\nPasswords, CSRF, sandbox  | Security\nREST API  | API-Inte